rs/agg-sharp/commit/678032abbd7f7a7fad6599a369cffe952e6427ed","commit_subject":"Switching to another application closes open popups on every host. SystemWindow.Deactivated is raised by each platform host when its window stops being the one the user is using - the mac host from windowDidResignKey:, the X11 host from a real FocusOut, the browser host from the canvas blurring (tab or browser switch), the WinForms host from LostFocus - and popups shown through ShowPopup (PopupMenu) and PopupWidget close on it unless something holds them open. It is a separate signal from focus because the hosts rightly disagree about focus: Windows clears agg's focus on deactivation, while a mac app keeps its text field focused across an app switch, so on the mac and in the browser menus used to stay open. Raised only with EnablePlatformWindowInput on, so parallel automation runs keep their menus. WindowDeactivationTests pins the menu and PopupWidget closing and text focus staying; BrowserSystemWindowTests pins the browser leg. An automation run turns the hosts' calls off (IPlatformWindow.EnablePlatformWindowDeactivation, scoped by the runner): it drives its window with simulated input, so the desktop handing key status elsewhere mid-test is not the user leaving - in full runs the mac host's windowDidResignKey: was closing menus MenusWindowTests and MenuTests had just opened. WindowDeactivationTests pins the runner's scope.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"microsoft/onnxruntime-genai","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-28T21:22:48Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"81ab94fb2b7035fed9de3487a34d1d2df5445e1e","github_link":"https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime-genai/commit/81ab94fb2b7035fed9de3487a34d1d2df5445e1e","commit_subject":"Restore DFlash2 drafting after exact prefix-cache hits (#2634)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"opsmill/infrahub","commit_timestamp":"2026-09-28T21:22:47Z","branch":"stable","commit_sha":"3e9ac0a48697d3d2464f597275558826c2adbe03","github_link":"https://github.com